From 118c2f137bfc4286d41af59cd1ec3be59e637b5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Ron D." <8740514+rgnv@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:44:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 22/29] net+menu: in-browser LAN discovery/join; robust WS
 transport

Browser multiplayer round-trip end-to-end (verified live): LAN refresh
-> server listed -> join -> lobby -> host presses Start in the setup
screen -> match loads and renders.

- cl_main: accept NA_BROADCAST 'info' replies (the WS bridge echoes our
  own broadcast destination as the packet source); add WC3_DebugMenuCommand
  (KEEPALIVE test hook to drive menu commands from the page); cl_timeout
  cvar (default 120s) replaces the fixed 10s netchan silence window that
  disconnected clients during cold real-data world loads.
- net.c: NET_WS_Open reuses the live bridge socket; reopening left
  net_ws_opened stale and sends threw InvalidStateError (uncaught page
  error, black canvas) whenever the engine reconfigured the transport
  (each LAN refresh).
- cl_parse: read the lobby host flag in its wire position (local_slot ->
  is_host -> revision); the misplaced read shifted the revision.
- sv_lobby: dedicated servers skip their boot-time loopback client when
  electing the lobby host (first remote player becomes host).
- bridge.mjs: --host listen address arg; run-dedicated-browser.sh: real
  data lobby, config-first command order, delayed until the console is
  free (pipe coalescing swallowed early commands during long loads).
- Makefile: export ccall/cwrap/stringToUTF8 runtime methods.
